  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CSF 10-22 Y3 PAYMENT - DELIVERY OF SUSTAINABLE AND QUALITY EYE HEALTH CARE AT</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To reduce the prevalence of avoidable blindness and visual impairment due to trachoma, cataract and refractive error (RE) in GGDKA-D in Ethiopia. These three leading causes of avoidable blindness in Ethiopia disproportionately affect rural women, girls, children and the elderly. Investment and interventions, supported by Irish Aid and Orbis Ireland, have reduced active and blinding trachoma prevalence, in fact 26% of targeted intervention districts are now below the World Health Organisation&#x2019;s (WHO) recommended cut-off levels. The project will continue to successfully implement the WHO&#x2019;s SAFE strategy (Surgery, Antibiotics, Facial cleanliness and Environmental improvement) by building on best practices and lessons learned since 2007.</narrative>
  </description>
